        },
        "justification": "The idea fundamentally changes the state of the oil upon breach, turning a catastrophic spill into a slow leak or solid mass. This excellent mitigation comes at the cost of high technical complexity and operational expenses (cooling or additives) which slightly affects transport continuity and feasibility.",
        "total": 550
